lox init: /project

Prerequisites
  ok  Docker 29.0.0
  ok  cosign (lox add and lox up verify every image's signature)
  ok  lea
  ok  launchers: locksql, lockmq, lockfile, lockhttp

Declared in .lockfamily/lockfamily.yaml (kept as they are)
  web          lockhttp, profile default

Detected (read only: .env*, compose*.yaml, config/; no secret is read or kept)
  1  PostgreSQL  host.docker.internal:55432  user shop, database shop, tls disable
       from compose.yaml (service db), .env (DATABASE_URL)
  2  RabbitMQ    http://host.docker.internal:55672  user orders, vhost orders, AMQP amqp://host.docker.internal:55673
       from compose.yaml (service mq)
  3  MySQL       inventory.internal:3307  user stock, database stock, tls verify-full
       from config/inventory.yaml

Auto (one lock per source above) or manual (a checklist)? a/m/q [a] 
Manual mode: what to set up (type numbers to toggle, Enter when done)
  1  [x] lea        runs the agents; they reach the locks
  2  [x] locksql    databases: PostgreSQL, MySQL, MariaDB, SQLite
  3  [x] lockmq     RabbitMQ: queues and streams
  4  [ ] lockfile   files: a local directory, S3, SFTP
  5  [ ] lockhttp   the web requests of lea's agents, held at lea's gate
  6  [-] locklog    not available yet: no release, and lox up does not run it
  declared in lockfamily.yaml (uncheck to remove; its profile stays in the lock's directory):
  7  [x] web        lockhttp, profile default
