locksql
  1) PostgreSQL host.docker.internal:55432 user shop, database shop, tls disable
  2) MySQL inventory.internal:3307 user stock, database stock, tls verify-full
  3) another
Which one? [1] Engine (postgres, mysql, mariadb, sqlite): [postgres] Host (host.docker.internal is this machine): [host.docker.internal] Port: [55432] User: [shop] Database: [shop] TLS (disable, prefer, require, verify-ca, verify-full): [disable] Instance name (lockfamily.yaml): [db] 
lockfile
Source (local, s3, sftp): [local] Directory (an absolute path): [/project] Instance name (lockfamily.yaml): [files] 
Environment of these locks: dev or prod? [dev] Passwords: asked by each console at its start (ask), or read from Vault (vault)? [ask] 
Plan (nothing is written before your yes)
  locksql orders
    locksql profile add --profile orders --production --credentials ask --engine postgres --host host.docker.internal --port 55432 --user shop --database shop --tls require
    then locksql init claude, locksql doctor, lox add locksql orders --profile orders
    allowed_uids [1000]: lea's agents run as uid 1000
  lockfile files
    lockfile profile add --profile files --production --source local --path /srv/shared
    then lockfile init claude, lockfile doctor, lox add lockfile files --profile files
    allowed_uids [1000]: lea's agents run as uid 1000
  remove: web (lockhttp) from lockfamily.yaml; its profile stays in .lockhttp/
Then lox up shows the whole change for your review: nothing starts without your yes there.
Go on? [y/N] 
locksql orders
  profile add: profile orders written to /project/.locksql/config.toml (credentials ask)
  init claude: the agent's files written
  doctor: 1 ok, 1 warning(s), 1 failed (advisory before lox up)
    project: owned by you (doctor --fix)
    lox init does not run locksql doctor --fix: it gives .locksql/ to the console account, and lox up copies a profile only from your own files
  lox add: lock orders declared
lockfile files
  profile add: profile files written to /project/.lockfile/config.toml
  init claude: the agent's files written
  doctor: 1 ok, 1 warning(s), 1 failed (advisory before lox up)
    project: owned by you (doctor --fix)
    lox init does not run lockfile doctor --fix: it gives .lockfile/ to the console account, and lox up copies a profile only from your own files
  lox add: lock files declared
removed web from lockfamily.yaml

lox up: review the change

Each console that started asks its questions here: its policy (y to approve it, on a first start) and the password it does not read from Vault (masked). Detach with Ctrl-P Ctrl-Q once it says Listening.



Run `lea` (or `claude` + `lox approve`).
